! mcp_bootstrap_p118.strap -- printed page 118, the tail of the
! "M ED" parameter-linkage loop, the whole of the "M TC" transfer-
! control / ENTER PSEUDO OP routine, three one-word constants, and
! the first three cards of S PRIME.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.125, header READ AND NOT ASSUMED:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID EA000050  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 118", read at
! 400 dpi with the words PAGE NUMBER in frame.
!
! FIFTY LINES, COUNTED NOT ESTIMATED.  The printed LINE column runs
! 1..50 with no gap and the form is blank below line 50.  The whole
! column was rendered and read in four bands at 400 dpi and again,
! column by column, in five bands at 900 dpi; nothing was read from
! band 1 alone.  The card-serial column runs EA000050 (line 1) to
! EA000098 (line 50) -- FORTY-NINE cards for fifty lines, because
! lines 26 and 27 ("MTC1 BUSAZ,$+.32" and the indented "BADZ,$+.32")
! share the serial EA000075: one card, two statements, two listed
! lines.  The header's CARD ID repeats line 1's serial.
!
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS NOT SET ON THIS PAGE. <<<  There is no SLC row
! here; line 1 is already at 215526.40 and the page runs contiguously
! to 215571.40.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! counter, and the VOLUME OCR of printed p.117 (a cross-check, never
! a source, and this page was not rendered) shows its last row as a
! half word at 215526.00 -- "000001.07 31  SV,2,1.0($1)" -- which
! ends exactly where line 1 begins.  The SLC card in this deck is the
! deck's own and is written "(8)215526.40": INSIDE AN (8) LITERAL
! BOTH PARTS ARE BASE 8, so the bit offset is the printed octal .40,
! not decimal 32.
!
! >>> TAIL SCOPE. <<<  pp.99+ are outside the TAIL,(2)G block that
! printed p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed, so a name here
! may repeat a name defined in pp.2-98 at a different address.  D MCP
! is exactly that: inside the tail it is 001472.00 (printed pp.91 and
! 97 both compile "B,DMCP" as "001472.10 00"), and out here it is
! 000040.00.  RECORDED, NOT "FIXED".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE DOES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! lines 1-24  build a TENTACLE ("TENT") entry for a linkage operation
!   and copy its parameters in.  The comments name every field:
!   "-**LINK FWA IN TENT**", "-**NORM. RET. ADR. IN TENT**", "-N IN
!   CF OF $1", "-***PARAM IN TENT."  M ED 1/M ED 1A is the copy loop
!   (load a 32-bit parameter progressively, store it, count the index
!   down, branch back on BXCZZ) and M ED 2A is a SWAPI pair around
!   S TLR+14.0 that swaps a register out and back.
! lines 25-44  the transfer-control block.  MR 3AD is a one half-word
!   cell, "-CURRENT TENTACLE TABLE ADDRESS", loaded into $1 by line
!   28 "-TRANSFER ROUTINES".  Lines 29-30 lift a 19-bit entry address
!   out of the table and plant it in M TC 3A, which is a "BD,$" --
!   the "- *****ENTER PSEUDO OP******" of line 40, a self-branch that
!   the preceding ST rewrites.  Lines 31-44 are the enable/disable
!   and SIO housekeeping around that entry: three BB tests on bits
!   .5/.6/.7 of the table entry, CM0000/CM1111 connectives that clear
!   or set the BD bit of M TC 3A and the SIO bit SPROGS+1.61, and a
!   TI that saves registers through S TLR+13.0.
! lines 45-47  three constants: M 9 (VF,.9), M KMCPA (a bare branch
!   to D MCP used as a transfer vector) and M MK 2, an indicator mask.
! lines 48-50  S PRIME begins -- "-SAVE X REGS. TO BE USED" into
!   M PR 8, then S PRIMR picks up the location of the "$ OP" and
!   loads its op code into $2.  The routine continues on printed
!   p.119, which is where M PR 8 (215622.00) and M C 1 (215637.00)
!   are defined.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LISTING MARKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every line number carries the ordinary asterisk ("1*", "50*").
! THREE lines carry a SECOND asterisk after the LOCATION -- lines 8,
! 26 and 39 -- the unexplained marker of docs/listing_typography.md
! 12.  printed p.112's deck tested and discarded the "SLC row" and
! "counter gap" readings of it; none of these three is an SLC row,
! none is at a counter gap, and all three carry ordinary binary
! (000021.34 80 / 215547.10 C6 / 215245.00 80).  Line 26 is also the
! first of the two statements that share one card, and line 8 and
! line 39 are not, so that is not it either.  LEFT OPEN, with nothing
! added to it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS THAT WERE AT RISK, AND HOW EACH WAS SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * "M ED 1" / "M ED 1A" / "M ED 2A" (lines 12, 14, 20).  Read at
!   1800 dpi: the D has the straight vertical left stem and squared
!   corners that a C and a 0 do not.  Corroborated two ways -- the
!   volume OCR spells "MED" twelve times and "MEO"/"M EO" zero times,
!   and line 16's own binary "215535.34 00" (BZB to M ED 1) pins
!   M ED 1 at 215535.00, which is line 12's location.
!   >>> THE VOLUME OCR IS WRONG ABOUT LINE 12. <<<  It reads line
!   12's NAME as "M C 1".  There IS a real M C 1 on this page, at
!   215637.00, referenced by line 15 -- a DIFFERENT symbol defined on
!   printed p.119.  The two must not be merged.
! * The byte of line 26, "215547.10 C6".  The C is open where the
!   same row's own octal ".10" prints a closed 0, so ink says
!   nothing.  SETTLED ON WHAT PRODUCED IT: BUSAZ is branch-on-
!   indicator USA (17) with the trailing-Z clear, and strap_asm
!   assembles "BUSAZ,$+.32" at 215546.40 to exactly 215547.10 C6.
!   Its neighbour "BADZ,$+.32" assembles to 215547.50 46, which is
!   the byte printed p.95/p.18 and many other decks already carry for
!   BADZ.
! * The byte of line 43, "215565.74 0E".  Settled from the BB_CODES
!   table in strap/opcodes.py before the ink was trusted: bits 60-61
!   are the "set afterward" modifier and bit 62 the tested value, so
!   BB is 02, BBZ is 06 and BB1 (mod 11, cond 1) is 0E.  This page
!   prints all three -- lines 31/33/34 are 02, line 41 is 06, line 43
!   is 0E -- and the assembler agrees with every one.
! * "MPR8" (line 48), not "MPRB".  Read at 1200 dpi; the glyph has
!   both bowls closed.  The volume OCR spells it MPR8 twice and MPRB
!   once, and printed p.119 line 40 defines it at 215622.00, which is
!   the address this row prints.
! * The comment of line 42 really is "-SAME ENABLDD".  Two D's, both
!   with left stems, at 1200 dpi.  The CARD is misspelled; it is
!   transcribed as printed.
! * Line 3's comment is "-ADDRESS OF LINKAGE OP": the O of its own
!   "OF" is open in the same word, so this row drops ink on round
!   glyphs, and "OP" is what lines 49 and 50 call the same thing
!   ("-PICK UP LOC. OF $ OP", "-OP CODE IN $2").
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ONE PRINTED FORM THIS DECK DOES NOT WRITE VERBATIM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 47 prints
!     M MK 2   INDMK,.21,.25,.26,.27,.28,.29,.30,.31,.55(.63)21
! and C28-6129 printed p.19 documents only "INDMK, A, B, C, D,....",
! each field NAMING ONE BIT.  "(.63)21" is a STRAP address-field
! notation this project has no source for, and strap_asm has no rule
! for it.  WHAT THE BITS SAY is unambiguous, because the MCP listing
! punches the same tail on three cards whose other fields differ:
!     p.118 l.47  M MK 2  .21,.25..31,.55(.63)21  000000.04 7F 000000.01 15
!     p.119       M MK 1  .53,.55(.63)21          000000.00 00 000000.05 15
!     p.119       M MK 3  .21,.55(.63)21          000000.04 00 000000.01 15
! (the two p.119 rows are read from the volume OCR, not transcribed).
! In all three, ".55(.63)21" contributes bits 55, 59, 61 and 63 and
! nothing else.  So this deck writes those four bits explicitly --
! ".55,.59,.61,.63" -- which assembles BIT-IDENTICALLY to the printed
! word, and the printed form is kept verbatim in the !CHECK note.
! WHAT IS STILL OPEN: the three cards cannot distinguish "bit .55
! plus the 8-bit field .56-.63 holding 0x15" from "bit .55 plus the
! value 21 right-justified at bit .63", because the bits between are
! zero either way.  No semantics is claimed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  Every address below is read off THIS page's own BINARY
! OUTPUT column, so a !CHECK on a row that uses one tests the opcode
! and modifier bits and not the address (listing_oracle's docstring).
! Each therefore carries its independent witness.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! STIC   215265.00 -- already SYN'd at this value by the p110, p111
!                     and p112 decks; here from lines 3 and 7
!                     ("215265.04 30" / "215265.05 30").
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
! STLR   215230.00 -- the volume OCR's printed p.117 line 12 is the
!                     defining card, "215230.00 * 000035.00  S T LR
!                     DRZ(BU,64),29".  This page agrees twice over:
!                     STLR+13.0 prints 215245.00 (line 39) and
!                     STLR+14.0 prints 215246.10 (lines 19, 21).
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
! SE     215001.00 -- printed p.103 line 10 defines it, "S E
!                     SYN(BU,1), S COM RG", and the p103 deck records
!                     215001.00+.  Here from lines 32 and 41.
SE      SYN, (8)215001.0
! SPROGS 215021.00 -- the p109 deck's !SYM carries 215021.00.  This
!                     page's lines 35 and 43 print SPROGS+1.61 as
!                     215022.75 (1 word + 61 decimal bits = .75
!                     octal), and printed p.117 line 46 prints
!                     SPROGS+1.25 as 215022.31.  Three offsets, one
!                     base.
SPROGS  SYN, (8)215021.0
! DMCP   000040.00 -- the p108 deck's "D MCP SYN,32.0" row IS the
!                     defining card (printed p.108 line 5, "000040.00+").
!                     The volume OCR shows about thirty "B,DMCP" rows
!                     at 22xxxx all printing "000040.10 00".  Written
!                     as a bare decimal 32.0 to match that deck.
DMCP    SYN, 32.0
! MPR8   215622.00 -- defined on printed p.119 (volume OCR line 40 of
!                     that page, "215622.00 *  M PR 8 DRZ(BU,...)"),
!                     and its "MPR8+1.0" on that same page prints
!                     215623.10.  Here from line 48.
MPR8    SYN, (8)215622.0
! MC1    215637.00 -- defined on printed p.119 (volume OCR line 4).
!                     Referenced from printed p.133 as well, which
!                     prints the same "215637.06 B0" this page's line
!                     15 prints.
MC1     SYN, (8)215637.0

! >>> TWO OF THE NAMES THIS PAGE *DEFINES* HAVE AN INDEPENDENT
! WITNESS, AND THEY AGREE. <<<  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p103.strap SYNs
! "SPRIME 215570.0" and "SPRIMR 215571.0" from printed pp.132/193
! ("B,SPRIME" printing 215570.10 and "SIC,SPRIMR" printing
! 215571.00) -- read by a different transcriber from different
! pages, and exactly the two locations lines 48 and 49 print here.
! tests/check_symbol_spellings.py was run with this deck alongside
! the repository's: 949 symbol definitions, none spelled two ways,
! and it groups this deck's STIC with pp.110/111/112, SE with p.103,
! SPROGS with p.109 and DMCP with p.108 at the same addresses.
! THE THREE WITH NO SECOND DECK are STLR, MPR8 and MC1; each rests
! on this page's binary plus the volume OCR of the page that defines
! it (printed p.117 line 12 for S TLR, printed p.119 for the other
! two), which is stated because the !CHECK rows that use them cannot
! test them.

        SLC, (8)215526.40
        SV,$2,2.0($1)                ! line  1 -**LINK FWA IN TENT**
        L(BU,4),0.0($1),-19          ! line  2
        LV,2,STIC                    ! line  3 -ADDRESS OF LINKAGE OP
        LV,4,$2                      ! line  4
        V+,$2,$L                     ! line  5 -RETURN ADDRESS IN $2
        SV,$2,1.32($1)               ! line  6 -**NORM. RET. ADR. IN TENT**
        SV,2,STIC                    ! line  7
        ST(BU,18),$1+.28,-19         ! line  8 -N IN CF OF $1
        LV,$3,$1                     ! line  9
        V+,$3,M9                     ! line 10
        V+I,$1,2.32                  ! line 11
MED1    L(V+I)(BU,32),.32($4)        ! line 12
        ST(V+IC)(BU,32),.32($1)      ! line 13 -***PARAM IN TENT.
MED1A   BXCZZ,MTC1                   ! line 14
        V+,$3,MC1                    ! line 15 -ADD. 2 FOR NEXT PARAM.
        BZB,0.0($3),MED1             ! line 16 -NO FORM EFF.
        SVA,4,MED2A                  ! line 17 -PARAM ADDR
        V+I,4,.32                    ! line 18
        SWAPI,4,$1,STLR+14.0         ! line 19
MED2A   LVE,$0,$                     ! line 20
        SWAPI,4,$1,STLR+14.0         ! line 21
        SV,0,0($1)                   ! line 22
        V+IC,1,.32                   ! line 23
        B,MED1A                      ! line 24
MR3AD   VF,0.0                       ! line 25 -CURRENT TENTACLE TABLE ADDRESS
MTC1    BUSAZ,$+.32                  ! line 26 \ one card, EA000075,
        BADZ,$+.32                   ! line 27 / two statements
        LV,$1,MR3AD                  ! line 28 -TRANSFER ROUTINES
        L(BU,19),.45($1)             ! line 29
        ST(BU,19),MTC3A              ! line 30 -SET ENTRY ADR.
MTC2A   BB,.5($1),MTC3B              ! line 31
        CM0000(BU,1),SE              ! line 32
        BB,.6($1),MTC3A-2.0          ! line 33 -ENTRY DISABLED
        BB,.7($1),MTC4A              ! line 34 -ENTRY SIO
        CM0000(BU,1),SPROGS+1.61     ! line 35 -TURN OFF SIO BIT FOR NEXT
!                                              M PACK
MTC3    CM0000(BU,1),MTC3A+.21       ! line 36
        B,MTC3A-1.0                  ! line 37 -TO ENABLED
        CM1111(BU,1),MTC3A+.21       ! line 38
        TI,0,STLR+13.0,$0            ! line 39
MTC3A   BD,$                         ! line 40 - *****ENTER PSEUDO OP******
MTC3B   BBZ,SE,MTC3A-2.0             ! line 41 -SAME DISABLED
        B,MTC3                       ! line 42 -SAME ENABLDD (as printed)
MTC4A   BB1,SPROGS+1.61,$+1.0        ! line 43 -TURN ON SIO BIT
        B,MTC3                       ! line 44 -SIO TO ENABLED
M9      VF,.9                        ! line 45
MKMCPA  B,DMCP                       ! line 46
! line 47 prints "INDMK,.21,.25,.26,.27,.28,.29,.30,.31,.55(.63)21".
! The last printed field is written out as its four bits; see above.
! The printed form assembles. This deck substituted
! ".55,.59,.61,.63" believing strap_asm had no rule for
! "(.63)21"; it does -- split_parenthetical_entries -- and the
! printed card compiles to 000000.04 7F 000000.01 15, which is
! what the page prints. Measured, not argued.
MMK2    INDMK,.21,.25,.26,.27,.28,.29,.30,.31,.55(.63)21
SPRIME  TI,5,$0,MPR8                 ! line 48 -SAVE X REGS. TO BE USED
SPRIMR  LVI,$1,0                     ! line 49 -PICK UP LOC. OF $ OP
        LV,$2,0.0($1)                ! line 50 -OP CODE IN $2

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
